  "asks": [
    {
      "id": "frag:q1",
      "question": "Who was Ysirveth, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "Some claim Ysirveth, god of harvest, plenty, and the debt of plenty, claimed a portion of the gift and took a throne. Of Ysirveth, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "frag:q2",
      "question": "Who was Quelmund, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "The tellings differ, but most agree Quelmund, god of healing and the price of healing, claimed a portion of the gift and took a throne. Of Quelmund, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "frag:q3",
      "question": "Who was Kamoth, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "The tellings differ, but most agree Kamoth the Unmarked, last-sworn of the Order of the Veil, set out for the place where Ysirveth was lost, carrying the order's final blessing. Of Kamoth, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "frag:q4",
      "question": "Who was Solendra, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "The tellings differ, but most agree the Church of Yoryne was raised at Velothasmere; Solendra of the Long Vigil took its first pulpit, preaching that the waning is a trial and the faithful will be spared. Of Solendra, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "frag:q5",
      "question": "Who was Serdis, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "The tellings differ, but most agree at the urging of Solendra, the saint Serdis the Kindly was given to the Sundered Moon in the rite of restoration. For a generation, the waning slowed. Of Serdis, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    },
    {
      "id": "frag:q6",
      "question": "Who was Nyessorn, and what became of them?",
      "fragment": "The tellings differ, but most agree Nyessorn the Lantern-eyed united the river-clans and was crowned in Hestvethshroud; the realm took the name Belthashollow. Of Nyessorn, the records otherwise keep their counsel.\n    \u2014 a marginal note, unsigned"
    }
  ],
